{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand","id":847667,"title":"Drive-Thru RPG - Damaged Goods. (Print on Demand)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-15T07:20:05-07:00","id":847667,"title":"Drive-Thru RPG - Damaged Goods. (Print on Demand)","content":"I've been ordering World of Darkness books from Drive-Thru RPG for about a year now, and 3 out of 4 of the &quot;Premium&quot; Full-Color Hardback books I've ordered from them were badly damaged/sabotaged upon arrival. Mainly, deep scratches and slashes on pages, creases, and so forth.<br /> <br /> Surely this is not normal, is it? According to a rep I spoke to, the books are printed by a third party, and I've asked them to look into any problems that might be going on at the printing end of things. Obviously they can't be selling inherently damaged and flawed goods to customers.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else had any experiences like this? All of the black &amp; white books I order have been fine so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:27:57-07:00","id":847673,"title":"","content":"My initial copy of TB:WH was imperfect. They replaced it immediately with no fuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:32:56-07:00","id":847675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=847673#post847673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial copy of TB:WH was imperfect. They replaced it immediately with no fuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I should explain in detail th history of my imperfect goods.<br /> <br /> 1. Ordered Vampire: The Requiem 2nd Edition Core Rulebook.(Premium Full-Color Hardback) which had a torn page somewhere in the middle. They replaced it with no fuss with a perfect copy.<br /> <br /> 2. Ordered The Danse Macabre.(Premium Full-Color Hardback) which had about 48 pages with scratches and creases. They sent me a replacement copy.<br /> <br /> 3. Replacement copy of The Danse Macabre arrived and was also riddled with scratches, creases and what appeared to be impact damage on the top right corner of many pages, as if the bundled pages has impacted a hard surface.<br /> <br /> That's 3 out of 4 supposedly &quot;Premium&quot; books which were damaged. I don't want to have to go through this every time I want to order Premium books from Drive-Thru. Like I said, they mentioned a third party, so I have asked them to look into it, and I may call this third party up myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:33:16-07:00","id":847677,"title":"","content":"I haven't ordered too many books from them, but my <i>Blood and Smoke: The Strix Chronicles</i>, <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken 2nd Edition</i>, <i>Geist: The Sin-Eaters</i>, <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, <i>God-Machine Chronicle</i>, and <i>Demon: The Descent</i> have all been in wonderful shape and mostly stayed that way (vampire and werewolf are a bit beat up at this point though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:58:28-07:00","id":847764,"title":"","content":"I suspect you're having a lot of misfortune. I've ordered a few books and they've been in good arrival condition, premium and softcover alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:05:35-07:00","id":847790,"title":"","content":"How weird. I've ordered more than a few books from them and the worst I've ever had was a crinkling at the top of a corner of the spine on the outside of the book that is, frankly, easily unnoticed. I've never heard of such a consistent stream of damaged goods going to the same person. You received these books in their packaging, unopened and untouched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:10:52-07:00","id":847814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=847790#post847790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How weird. I've ordered more than a few books from them and the worst I've ever had was a crinkling at the top of a corner of the spine on the outside of the book that is, frankly, easily unnoticed. I've never heard of such a consistent stream of damaged goods going to the same person. You received these books in their packaging, unopened and untouched?</div> </div> </div> </div>They appear to have been un-opened and un-touched, yes. Here are some photos I took of some instances of damage from the latest book. I will see about digging up the photos I took of the older damaged books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Drive-Thru are in the process of investigating these incidents and have been very curteous and professional in their handling of my queries and complaints. As long as everything is eventually in order, I don't mind waiting for however long it takes to resolve the problem. What is imediately bothering me though is that I now have a bunch of damaged Vampire: The Requiem books lying around, including at least 2 copies of The Danse Macabre. What the hell am I going to do with these? I could never bring myself to just destroy a book. :/<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:21:11-07:00","id":847825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Proteus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=847814#post847814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They appear to have been un-opened and un-touched, yes. Here are some photos I took of some instances of damage from the latest book. I will see about digging up the photos I took of the older damaged books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5089.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5091.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i752.photobucket.com/albums/xx164/Evil_Emperor_Proteus/IMG_5092.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Drive-Thru are in the process of investigating these incidents and have been very curteous and professional in their handling of my queries and complaints. As long as everything is eventually in order, I don't mind waiting for however long it takes to resolve the problem. What is imediately bothering me though is that I now have a bunch of damaged Vampire: The Requiem books lying around, including at least 2 copies of The Danse Macabre. What the hell am I going to do with these? I could never bring myself to just destroy a book. :/<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could gift them to your players who don't have copies and aren't willing to shell out the money themselves if they're okay with the damage. I once gladly accepted a gift of a NWoD core book that was missing the cover. Would help with the bookkeeping at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T14:56:12-07:00","id":847880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=847825#post847825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could gift them to your players who don't have copies and aren't willing to shell out the money themselves if they're okay with the damage. I once gladly accepted a gift of a NWoD core book that was missing the cover. Would help with the bookkeeping at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could also gift them to your local library and thus encourage more gaming in the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T02:00:41-07:00","id":848052,"title":"","content":"I'm one of those lucky few who hears about damaged books from DTRPG, but has yet to receive one in less than perfect condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T03:58:53-07:00","id":848071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=848052#post848052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one of those lucky few who hears about damaged books from DTRPG, but has yet to receive one in less than perfect condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>DriveThru outright said to me during my inquiry that the books are printed by a third party. I'm from the UK and the books I get are printed in the UK, so I think they might commission the books from local sources depending on the location of the buyer. I might just be unfortunate enough to have gotten a printer who is having problems printing the premium full-color books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T04:09:45-07:00","id":848073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Proteus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=848071#post848071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DriveThru outright said to me during my inquiry that the books are printed by a third party. I'm from the UK and the books I get are printed in the UK, so I think they might commission the books from local sources depending on the location of the buyer. I might just be unfortunate enough to have gotten a printer who is having problems printing the premium full-color books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also UK-based. I believe the books are produced by Lightning Source, but don't quote me on that. I got my Requiem 2nd, Mummy sourcebooks, and some of the blue books through them in premium, without difficulty. The issues would seem to occur on and off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:37:42-07:00","id":848153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/847667-drive-thru-rpg-damaged-goods-print-on-demand?p=847880#post847880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could also gift them to your local library and thus encourage more gaming in the world.</div> </div> </div